WHY BOTH, since a single licence would be less paperwork. The protocol core
is Rust, where offering both is the ecosystem's convention and the thing
contributors and reimplementers expect to find. It is also strictly more
permissive for a recipient than either alone: anyone who wants the express
patent grant takes the Apache arm, anyone who wants the shorter and more
widely understood terms takes MIT, and — the reason that actually decided it
— Apache-2.0 on its own is incompatible with GPLv2, which would have quietly
excluded a class of downstream projects from ever using this at all.

SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT OR Apache-2.0

CONTRIBUTIONS. Unless you state otherwise, any contribution intentionally
submitted for inclusion in this work shall be dual-licensed as above, with no
additional terms or conditions.
